{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,12]],"date-time":"2026-08-12T22:45:03Z","timestamp":1786574703006,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":17,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"4","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2008,3,12]],"date-time":"2008-03-12T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1205280000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":71,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Biopharm &amp; Drug Disp"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2008,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>It has been reported that tamoxifen is a substrate of P\u2010glycoprotein (P\u2010gp) and microsomal cytochrome P450 (CYP) 3A, and kaempferol is an inhibitor of P\u2010gp and CYP3A. Hence, it could be expected that kaempferol would affect the pharmacokinetics of tamoxifen. Thus, tamoxifen was administered orally (10\u2009mg\/kg) without or with oral kaempferol (2.5 and 10\u2009mg\/kg). In the presence of kaempferol, the total area under the plasma concentration\u2013time curve from time zero to time infinity (<jats:italic>AUC<\/jats:italic>) of tamoxifen was significantly greater, <jats:italic>C<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>max<\/jats:sub> was significantly higher and <jats:italic>F<\/jats:italic> was considerably greater than those without kaempferol. The enhanced bioavailability of oral tamoxifen by oral kaempferol could have been due to an inhibition of CYP3A and P\u2010gp by kaempferol. The presence of kaempferol did not alter the pharmacokinetic parameters of a metabolite of tamoxifen, 4\u2010hydroxytamoxifen. This could have been because the contribution of CYP3A to the formation of 4\u2010hydroxytamoxifen is not considerable in rats. Copyright \u00a9 2008 John Wiley &amp; Sons, Ltd.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/bdd.593","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2008,3,12]],"date-time":"2008-03-12T16:48:05Z","timestamp":1205340485000},"page":"245-249","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":31,"title":["Effects of oral kaempferol on the pharmacokinetics of tamoxifen and one of its metabolites, 4\u2010hydroxytamoxifen, after oral administration of tamoxifen to rats"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"29","author":[{"given":"Yongji","family":"Piao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Sang\u2010Chul","family":"Shin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jun\u2010Shik","family":"Choi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2008,3,12]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_1_2_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1124\/dmd.105.005611"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_3_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/tx010125x"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_4_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1200\/JCO.1995.13.2.513"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_5_2","first-page":"451","article-title":"Tamoxifen: a reappraisal of its pharmacodynamic and pharmacokinetic properties, and therapeutic use","volume":"37","author":"Buckley MT","year":"1989","journal-title":"Clin Pharmacokinet"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_6_2","first-page":"645","article-title":"Metabolism of the antimammary cancer antiestrogenic agent tamoxifen, I. Cytochrome P450\u2010catalysed N\u2010demethylation and 4\u2010hydroxylation","volume":"21","author":"Mani C","year":"1993","journal-title":"Drug Metab Dispos"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_7_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0006-2952(96)00650-8"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_8_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0006-2952(94)90099-X"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_9_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/jf000892m"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_10_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1211\/0022357056299"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_11_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.101